# Always open a PR

When you finish a change set that should land in the repo (features, fixes, website/docs, iOS, Supabase), **do not stop at a local commit or a pushed branch**.

## Required finish line

1. Commit on a feature branch (never commit straight to `main` unless the user explicitly says so).
2. Push the branch to `origin`.
3. Open a pull request with `gh pr create` (title + summary + test plan).
4. Return the **PR URL** in your reply to the user.

## Website / `docs/` changes

Treat GitHub Pages / `docs/` the same as app code: every website change ships as a PR (or a stacked series of PRs). Do not leave website work only on the working tree.

## If `gh` is not authenticated

- Attempt `gh auth status`.
- If logged out, tell the user once to run `gh auth login` (or provide `GH_TOKEN`), then retry `gh pr create`.
- Still push the branch so compare links work, but keep trying to create the PR — compare links alone are not the finish line.

## Split work

Prefer small, reviewable PRs. When splitting, open every PR in the stack, not just the tip.
